%U A400600 67108562,134217401,268435103,536870532,1073741416,2147483211,4294966829,8589934094,17179868654,34359737805
%N A400600 Largest m such that one defective in an m-item set and one in a disjoint 5-item set can always be identified in at most n adaptive tests, each returning the number of defectives in a selected subset (0 if no positive m is feasible).
%H A400600 S. Li, X. Wu and E. Triesch, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.dam.2018.05.026">A ternary search problem on two disjoint sets</a>, Discrete Applied Mathematics 251 (2018), 221-235.
%F A400600 Let f(n) = 2^n - n*(n-3)/2 - 5. Then a(n) = f(n) for 2 <= n <= 8; a(n) = f(n)+1 for 9 <= n <= 10; a(n) = f(n)+2 for n >= 11 (for n >= 3, see Li, Wu and Triesch, Theorems 1-3 and Remark 1).
%Y A400600 Cf. A000079, A000225, A000325, A132824, A400594, A400595.
%K A400600 nonn,easy,new
